			<editorialDecl><p>This transcription was made on a Vulgate base text, from a copy of Dold's article in Georg Leyh (ed.), Aus der Welt des Buches (Zentralblatt für Bibliothekswesen Beiheft 75). Leipzig: Otto Harrassowitz, 1950, pp. 13–29. It only comprises the Latin pages of this Latin-Gothic bilingual. This transcription includes all page layout information, formatting, punctuation, abbreviations, digraphs, corrections. There appears not to be any punctuation in the form of dots, despite Dold's text of fol 280r, only diplai and paragraph marks (a line in the left margin above the ekthetic initial). A different abbreviation symbol is used for 'm' and 'n', the former with a dot. Word divisions correspond to the Vulgate base text (only affects idipsum). The extant portions of the MS are Romans 11:33–12:5; 12:17–13:5; 14:9–20; 15:3–13. The transcriber was Hugh Houghton in June 2013; the transcription was proofread by Hugh Houghton in May 2014 on the basis of new colour images from the HAB Wolfenbuettel website and an online transcription by Falluomini <ptr target="http://diglib.hab.de/edoc/ed000006/index.php?transcript=palimpsest_Ulfilas_Falluomini"/>. The latter is not always an improvement on Dold, e.g. erroneous addition of 'matis' on 255r line 26 and omission of 'tibi' on 280r line 3.</p> <p>The proofread plain text file was converted to XML in October 2014. The original transcription guidelines can be found at <ptr target="http://epapers.bham.ac.uk/1676/"/></p>
				<p>The XML specifications used are version 1.5 of the IGNTP Guidelines available at <ptr target="http://epapers.bham.ac.uk/1892/"/></p></editorialDecl>
